WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.870
In the 1960s and 70s, a new wave of
feminism changed women's roles in work,

2
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.840
law and education.

3
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.350
Many Jewish women asked why their
religious lives had not changed too.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.360
The theologian Judith
Plaskow went further.

5
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:20.650
Even at Sinai, she argued, women
were present but left unaddressed.

6
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.510
If women were left out
of the story at Sinai,

7
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.130
can Jewish tradition be
retold without breaking it?

8
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.010
In this mission, you'll see how traditional
Jewish marriage can leave a wife chained,

9
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.400
and how Rachel Adler responds.

10
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.100
Then you'll weigh Orthodox and
Progressive responses to these new ideas.

11
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.860
Your mission: weigh up whether Jewish
tradition can be retold to include women

12
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.170
without breaking it.
